/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Interpretation There are no strong linear relationships between the measured variables, which indicates that network performance depends on multiple independent factors rather than direct pairwise relations. The weak correlation between signal-related metrics \(Signal Strength, SNR, Attenuation\) may suggest variability due to environmental or temporal factors not captured in the dataset. This analysis helps confirm that further modeling \(e.g., Machine Learning\) should rely on non-linear methods to capture complex interactions.)
